 - **Hub sync commits returned deletions after a partial Git add failure** (V-1092; `app/hub_workspace.py`). When an ignored return path makes a batch add fail after staging other paths, the fallback retains returned deletions already in the index instead of retrying them as missing pathspecs and leaving them outside the commit. Unrelated staged native edits stay outside the commit; ignored files remain ignored. Regression coverage includes deletion-only and mixed returns, pre-staged deletions, native index preservation and repeated unchanged snapshots. Python change follows the normal service lifecycle.
 - **ElevenLabs Flash narration defaults to the owner's saved Sergey voice** (V-1086; `scripts/video_artifact/make.py`, `elevenlabs_tts.py`). RU/EN HTML and Manim builds now use `eleven_flash_v2_5` and configurable voice `XuEV9VY3VUASYgJVNBh0`; Tera/Vosk/Kokoro remain explicit local choices. A small text/file CLI shares the same cache and MP3-to-48-kHz-WAV path. Cache keys include text/model/voice/settings/language, never credentials. Local pause samples preserve timing, preview and check-only never submit speech, and durable request markers prevent replay after uncertain failures; received audio survives decoder failures. No automatic provider/model fallback or generation retry. Root verified the account's character multiplier of 0.5; live audio and host acceptance remain separate. Canonical skill edits are assigned to native worker V-1088; integration text and verification limits are in `.orchestra/tasks/V-1086/report.md`.
 ### Fixed
+- **Error-watch ignores Hub's missing owned_dirs guard refusal** (V-1116; `app/error_watch.py`). Only the refusal explaining that a worker has no `owned_dirs` and whole-project uploads require a persistent project is classified as noise, including normalized signatures, and excluded from post-fix recurrence counts. Hub sync size-limit failures and other hub turn failures remain actionable. Upload guards are unchanged. Standalone cron imports the change on its next run.
 - **Error-watch ignores intermediate hub watch read retries** (V-1115; `app/error_watch.py`). Only `hub t3_thread_wait/read failed; retrying in ...s: ...` messages are classified as noise, including normalized delay values. Final exceptions and `hub watch request exceeded 60 seconds` remain actionable. Retry behavior is unchanged. Standalone cron imports the change on its next run.
 - **Error-watch ignores Bash's standalone child-termination message** (V-1111; `app/error_watch.py`). Only `logs` / `tool_result` / `Bash` events whose raw content strips to exactly `Terminated` are classified as noise. Other tools and longer messages remain actionable, even alongside identical noise signatures. Standalone cron imports the change on its next run.
 - **Past quota-chart cycles show the threshold the gate really applied, not one stretched to the next reset** (V-1108; `app/static/js/quota-lines.js`, `_qlResetCycles`). V-1105 made the chart start a new curve after an early reset, but each earlier cycle was still compressed to reach the ceiling exactly at the next actual reset. The gate never knew that reset: `window_progress` uses the `resets_at` of that moment over the full `window_minutes`. Each reset event now carries the `resets_at` seen just before it, and a past cycle's progress runs over the full window from that `resets_at`, so the curve stops at the early reset at its real progress (a reset after ~1 day of 7 ends at ~1/7, not at the ceiling). The current-window projection is unchanged. Live check against `usage_snapshots` 23–27.10: chart and `line_limit` agree at every sampled snapshot (table in `.orchestra/tasks/V-1108/report.md`). Gate policy unchanged, JS only, no restart. Regression: `tests/test_quota_reset_restart_1105.py`; `test_codex_threshold_uses_observed_boundaries_after_early_reset` previously asserted the stretched curve and now asserts the gate progress.
